  "notes": "REBUILT 2026-09-18 by QA reviewer #3 -- the prior version of this file (an earlier Haiku-tier agent's output) claimed to be 'generated from bulletin_scraper.py output for archive year 2023' but its actual semester-by-semester content did not match the real scraper output at all: it had a 9-semester/132-credit structure where courses were assigned to the WRONG semesters relative to what the 2023 archived bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan table shows (verified by re-running `python3 bulletin_scraper.py \\\"https://bulletins.psu.edu/undergraduate/colleges/behrend/interdisciplinary-science-business-bs/\\\" 2023 2026` directly), and its Quantitative/Technical-Sales module elective codes (STAT 461/462, MKTG 410, SCM 455/460, CMPSC options, DIGIT 410, ECON 481/485, MATH 482, MIS 315/336/345, STAT 318/414/464/466, MIS 404, MKTG 485, ACCTG 340) were copied from ISB-2026.json's own Program-Notes-derived module picks without any citation confirming those same footnote module lists applied in 2023 -- bulletin_scraper.py only parses the plan GRID, not the Program Notes footnote text, so that specific claim was never actually scraper-verified for this year, just assumed.\n\nThis rebuild instead: (1) uses the real per-year scraped grid content and ordering (all four years 2022-2025 have an IDENTICAL underlying plan-grid: MATH140/110, BIOL110, CHEM110&111, ENGL15/30H, PSU7 in term 1; STAT200/250/SCM200, PHYS250(or CHEM112&113), ECON102, MIS204, and a CAS-writing-course in term 2; etc. -- confirmed identical via direct scraper re-run for each year), (2) keeps the SAME MATH 21 -> MATH 22 -> CHEM 110/ACCTG 211 remediation detour that ISB-2026.json's own notes document as a real, necessary hard-prereq-gap workaround (CHEM 110's catalog prereq is MATH 22, not the MATH 140/110 this major's own Gen Ed math satisfies; ACCTG 211 needs MATH 21) -- MATH 21/22 are real Penn State courses, just not printed as their own line in the bulletin's Suggested Academic Plan grid (the bulletin assumes math placement testing out), same convention documented independently for ABSM/ACCTG/LSCPE/NUTR's identical gap, and (3) leaves the Science/Business Module slots GENERIC (not tied to specific elective codes) since only the plan grid, not that year's own Program Notes page, was actually scraper-verified here -- this is the scraper's own is_generic_slot=true treatment for that grid position in every year checked. Total credits: 132 (matches ISB-2026.json's own 132, i.e. the printed 125-129 range plus the same 6cr MATH 21/22 remediation 2026 already documents needing).\n\nSource (this year's real archive page): https://bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2023-2024/undergraduate/colleges/behrend/interdisciplinary-science-business-bs/",
